# =============================================================================
# ICA 2026 — "From Diagnosis to Decision"
#
# Boundary rule: the repository carries SCIENTIFIC CODE and REPRODUCIBILITY
# ARTIFACTS (manifests, indexes, mappings, exclusions, reports). It never
# carries raw or licensed dataset pixels, archives, caches, or credentials.
#
# Ignored files are NOT deleted locally — they simply stay untracked.
# =============================================================================

# --- raw image data: never committed (licensing + size) ----------------------
# PlantVillage is CC BY-SA 3.0 and PlantDoc CC BY 4.0, but neither is
# redistributed here; see DATA_ACCESS.md for local placement.
data/raw/

# --- data/interim: derived scratch, EXCEPT the Phase-1 validation outputs ----
# Contents are excluded with `/*` (not `dir/`) so the negations below can still
# re-include individual reproducibility-critical files. `dir/` would make the
# re-inclusions unreachable.
data/interim/*
!data/interim/phase1_review_validation.csv
!data/interim/phase1_review_validation_summary.json

# --- superseded / regenerable report artifacts -------------------------------
# Contact sheets are ~4.1 MB of derived collages regenerable from raw data via
# `python scripts/prepare_human_review.py`; the reviewer uses them locally.
reports/near_duplicate_contact_sheets/
# Same policy for the PlantDoc duplicate packet: the CSV/JSON/Markdown evidence
# and decision forms ARE tracked, but the ~1.7 MB of rendered collages are
# regenerable via `python scripts/build_plantdoc_duplicate_packet.py`. Their
# SHA-256 values stay recorded in packet_manifest.json.
reports/plantdoc_exact_duplicate_review/*.png
# Legacy CPU smoke-run figures, superseded and not referenced by any report.
reports/_legacy_smoke_figures/
# Point-in-time remediation backups (local history only).
reports/_remediation_backup_*/

# --- credentials / secrets (double-blind submission + security) --------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
kaggle.json
.kaggle/
.huggingface/
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.*
*_secret*
hf_token*
credentials.json
service_account*.json

